explain format=tree select id from sbtest1 where k = 111 and k2 in (110, 111, 112) and id > 3 order by id limit 2, 10;
EXPLAIN
-> Limit/Offset: 10/2 row(s)  (cost=1.46 rows=4)
    -> Sort: sbtest1.id, limit input to 12 row(s) per chunk  (cost=1.46 rows=6)
        -> Filter: ((sbtest1.k = 111) and (sbtest1.k2 in (110,111,112)) and (sbtest1.id > 3))  (cost=1.46 rows=6)
            -> Covering index range scan on sbtest1 using k_1 over (k = 111 AND k2 = 110 AND 3 < id pushed_limit 12) OR (k = 111 AND k2 = 111 AND 3 < id pushed_limit 12) OR (k = 111 AND k2 = 112 AND 3 < id pushed_limit 12)  (cost=1.46 rows=6)

select id from sbtest1 where k = 111 and k2 in (110, 111, 112) and id > 3 order by id limit 2, 10;
